review / review	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-08-15T04:56:08.6250274Z ## Failures
review / review	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-08-15T04:56:08.6252589Z **verification_explanation_quality (FAIL).** The `verification_explanation` in `task.toml` (line 18) is stale relative to the shipped verifier. It explicitly says the verifier "Verifies exact match ... across **11 orders**" and "order count of **11**," and gives a processing sequence of exactly 11 orders (`O00_A, O00_B, O00_C, O00_D, O00_E, O01, O03, O02, O04, O05, O06`). But `tests/test_outputs.py` asserts `len(orders) == 19` (line 23) and hardcodes expected values for eight additional orders — O00_F, O00_G, O00_H, O00_I, O00_J, O00_K, O00_L, O00_M (test functions lines 142–201) — none of which the explanation mentions. The explanation therefore both states a wrong count and fails to describe what roughly 40% of the assertions check. The contributor must rewrite `verification_explanation` to match the current 19-order test suite: correct the count/processing order and describe what each of the O00_F–O00_M checks verifies (scrap ceiling, WC setup+run hours, initial-vs-leftover limiting-resource calc, substitute integer conversion, sub-assembly exclusion, child-SA batch rounding, ceil on scrap %).
review / review	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-08-15T04:56:08.6254183Z 
